<title>USA: Consolidated Freightways unit spinoff OK'd.</title>
<headline>Consolidated Freightways unit spinoff OK'd.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Freightways Inc said the U.S. Internal Revenue Service has approved the tax-free spin-off of the company's long-haul motor carrier as a separate publicly traded company.</p>
<p>Consolidated Freightways announced plans to spin off the subsidiary in August.  It said the new company will be called Consolidated Freightways Corp, and the parent will change its name to CNF Transportation Inc.</p>
<p>It said Wednesday that it expects the spinoff to be completed in November.</p>
</text>
